---
description: Reconcile a close assertion through source lineage, break ownership and independent signoff.
args: { request: CloseCycleRequest; books: CloseSourceBook }
returns: CloseProgramResult
uses: [closeDesk/traceCloseAssertion, closeDesk/classifyLedgerBreaks, closeDesk/commissionBreakOwners, closeDesk/assembleWorkpaperConclusion, closeDesk/checkIndependentSignoff, closeDesk/invalidateLateJournalScope, closeDesk/compareRegeneratedSource, closeDesk/quarantineBrokenFormula, closeDesk/recordMissedDeadline]
---
1. Bind saved = books.checkpoint when present, otherwise null. Initialize breaks = null, taskQueue = null, conclusion = null and signoffReview = null. Treat every workpaper as an assertion over one entity, period, account set and immutable source editions.
2. Bind scope = traceCloseAssertion(request, books.workpapers, books.evidencePages). Bind journalImpact = invalidateLateJournalScope(request, books.lateJournalReceipts, books.priorSignoffs), regeneration = compareRegeneratedSource(request, books.reportRegenerations), formulaGate = quarantineBrokenFormula(request, books.formulaValidationReceipts), and deadlineState = recordMissedDeadline(request, books.deadlineEvents). Keep changed-line findings even when aggregate totals agree. Formula-derived amounts require a matching validation receipt for the exact formula, input range and output.
3. When scope has all required accounts, exact source editions and no unresolved scope blockers, and formulaGate has no unresolved computed amount, bind breaks = classifyLedgerBreaks(scope, books.evidencePages). Keep offsetting source lines separate. Otherwise retain null breaks and explain the blocked examination in scope or formulaGate; no examined-account or completed-queue claim is permitted.
4. When breaks exists, bind taskQueue = commissionBreakOwners(request, breaks, books.preparerTransfers). An examined, complete ledger with no material unresolved fact yields {tasks: [], unassignedBreakIds: [], openEvidenceNeeds: [], complete: true}. An incomplete ledger cannot produce that clean queue. A successor receives an open task without rewriting its original preparer or missed deadline.
5. When breaks and taskQueue exist and every required evidence task has completion evidence, bind conclusion = assembleWorkpaperConclusion(scope, breaks, taskQueue, books.evidencePages). Keep verified facts, management explanations and residual amounts separate. A material unsupported residual prevents a clean conclusion even when all tasks were attempted.
6. Only when conclusion exists and its residual schedule is complete, bind signoffReview = checkIndependentSignoff(request, scope, conclusion, books.priorSignoffs). Bind reviewer eligibility to exact source-line and conclusion versions and require a reviewer distinct from the preparer. An eligibility review never becomes a captured signature.
7. Bind checkpoint = reconcileCloseCheckpoint(saved, request, books, scope, breaks, taskQueue, conclusion, signoffReview). Preserve every workpaper edition and journal receipt; source changes reopen only consuming assertions. Return { caseId: request.caseId, scope, breaks, tasks: taskQueue, conclusion, signoff: signoffReview, guardrails: [journalImpact, regeneration, formulaGate, deadlineState], checkpoint, commitAllowed: false } as CloseProgramResult. This same complete shape covers missing sources, unresolved breaks and signoff-ready workpapers. Posting journals and recording signatures require their actual authorized operations.
